<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01UF">Remark <span data-tag="01UF">5.1.4.6</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a pullback diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ X' \ar [r]^-{f} \ar [d]^-{q'} &amp;  X \ar [d]^-{q} \\ S' \ar [r] &amp;  S. } \]
</div>
<p> If $q$ is a cartesian fibration, then $q'$ is also a cartesian fibration. Moreover, an edge $e'$ of $X'$ is $q'$-cartesian if and only if $e = f(e')$ is a $q$-cartesian edge of $X$ (this follows from Remarks <a data-tag="01UE" href="/tag/01UE">5.1.4.5</a> and <a data-tag="01U2" href="/tag/01U2">5.1.3.5</a>). Similarly, if $q$ is a cocartesian fibration, then $q'$ is also a cocartesian fibration (and an edge $e'$ of $X'$ is $q'$-cocartesian if and only if $e = f(e')$ is a $q$-cocartesian edge of $X$). </p>
</article>
